  "notes": "UTG limps for 2 and it folds to hero on the button. A limp is the one preflop action that caps a range: almost nobody limps aces. So the button attacks it with a very wide raising range, and the isolation raise — not the call — is the point. Calling invites the blinds in behind and turns a heads-up pot in position into a four-way one.",
